subproblem.statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ and ρ ∈ ℝ. Let G : ℝ^n → ℝ^P be measurable, H : ℝ^{n+1} → ℝ^P any map, A ⊆ ℝ^n Borel, and w : ℝ^n → ℤ and c : ℝ^n → ℝ measurable. Assume (w : ℝ) is Lebesgue integrable on A, ‖G(u)‖ ≤ ρ for u ∈ A, and for every u ∈ A: c(u) ≥ 0 and |α(DG(u)e_0, …, DG(u)e_{n−1})| ≤ c(u)·|α| for every n-covector α on ℝ^P (|α| = covectorEuclideanNorm α). Write z_0 := WithLp.ofLp z 0 and tail z := WithLp.toLp 2 (Fin.tail (WithLp.ofLp z)), and let B := {z ∈ ℝ^{n+1} : z_0 ∈ (0, 1) and tail z ∈ A}. Assume that for every z ∈ B the tuple (b ↦ DH(z)ê_b) equals Fin.cons (G(tail z)) (a ↦ z_0·DG(tail z)e_a). Put c′(z) := z_0^n·‖G(tail z)‖·c(tail z). Then:
(i) z ↦ (w(tail z) : ℝ) is integrable on B;
(ii) for every z ∈ B, c′(z) ≥ 0 and |α(DH(z)ê_0, …, DH(z)ê_n)| ≤ c′(z)·|α| for every (n+1)-covector α on ℝ^P;
(iii) ∫⁻_{z ∈ B} ofReal(|w(tail z)|·c′(z)) dz ≤ ofReal(ρ)·∫⁻_{u ∈ A} ofReal(|w(u)|·c(u)) du.
Here D = fderiv ℝ, e_a := EuclideanSpace.single a 1 ∈ ℝ^n, ê_b := EuclideanSpace.single b 1 ∈ ℝ^{n+1}, and all measures are Lebesgue measure.
